    "content": "\"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.\nItems, one per line:\np1:c1: The reference GISMo training command fixes the ingredient-encoder width at 300 dimensions (`hidden=300 emb_d=300`), with 2 GIN layers, 400 epochs and regular negative sampling — the single width the card would vary. | source: https://github.com/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/gismo/README.md | recorded quote: \\\"python train.py name=GIN_MLP setup=context-full max_context=43 \\ lr=0.00005 w_decay=0.0001 hidden=300 emb_d=300 dropout=0.25 \\ nr=400 nlayers=2 lambda_=0.0 i=1 init_emb=random \\ with_titles=False with_set=True filter=False\\\"\np1:c2: GISMo's published Recipe1MSubs test result — MRR 31.51 and Hit@1 20.56, averaged over 5 runs — is the exact baseline the card's 'Check first' reproduction targets. | source: https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2302.07960 | recorded quote: \\\"Table 1: Test results on Recipe1MSubs. Our method outperforms the baselines on all metrics. Results are averaged over 5 runs, and the mean ± std are reported. ... GISMo (Ours) 31.51±0.10 20.56±0.14 35.89±0.16 54.27±0.19\\\"\np1:c3: The model is implemented in PyTorch with the Deep Graph Library (DGL) for