reimplemented GISMo baseline scores Hit@1 34.53 ± 0.10% on the original Recipe1MSubs, and fine-tuned GPT-3.5-Turbo-1106 lifts this to 38.03 ± 0.28%, while TinyLlama-1.1B reaches only 20.93 ± 0.29%. | source: https://www.mdpi.com/2504-4990/6/4/131 | recorded quote: \\\"On the original and filtered dataset, the Hit@1 accuracy was 34.53 ± 0.10% and 40.24 ± 0.36%, respectively. ... Subsequent experiments with fine-tuned LLMs on the original GISMo ingredient substitution dataset yielded Hit@1 values of 20.09 ± 0.31% for DaVinci-002, 20.93 ± 0.29% for TinyLlama-1.1B, and 38.03 ± 0.28% for GPT-3.5-Turbo-1106.\\\"\np2:c3: The work sits inside the Hyperfoods ERC programme (coordinated by Imperial College London), which applies graph-based ML to computationally design personalised nutrition and which funded Rita et al. | source: https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/899932 | recorded quote: \\\"Hyperfoods will use novel graph-based ML methods to provide the technological capabilities for the computational discovery and design of personalised nutrition.\\\"\np2:c4: The re-run GISMo and fine-tuned models (plus the dataset-filtering and fine-tuning scripts) are released on the iAnalytica Bitbucket repository, so the card's width-sweep could be reproduced against their released baseline. | source: https://www.mdpi.com/2504-4990/6/4/131 | recorded quote: \\\"the fine-tuned models GISMo and TinyLlama, along with the scripts used for filtering the Recipe1MSubs dataset and fine-tuning the GISMo, DaVinci, GPT-3.5, and TinyLlama models, are hosted on the Bitbucket repository.\\\"\np2:done: Rita et al. re-implemented GISMo at a single 300-dim embedding width (averaged over 5 runs) and swept model families (DaVinci/TinyLlama/GPT-3.5), but never swept the GISMo encoder width across 64–512. | source: https://www.mdpi.com/2504-4990/6/4/131 | recorded quote: \\\"used an embedding dimension of 300 to represent ingredients in a continuous vector space. The model consists of two graph convolutional layers, each with 300 hidden units\\\"\nReturn only JSON: {\\\"items\\\": [{\\\"ref\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"SUPPORTED | PARTIAL | UNSUPPORTED | CONTRADICTED | UNREACHABLE\\\", \\\"page_quote\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"note\\\": \\\"\\\"}]}\""
