g\n\n### Forks\n\n[**5** forks](/facebookresearch/gismo/forks)\n\n[Report repository](/contact/report-content?content_url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Ffacebookresearch%2Fgismo&report=facebookresearch+%28user%29)\n\nmain\n\n[Branches](/facebookresearch/gismo/branches)[Tags](/facebookresearch/gismo/tags)\n\n[](/facebookresearch/gismo/branches)[](/facebookresearch/gismo/tags)\n\nGo to file\n\nCode\n\nOpen more actions menu\n\n## Latest commit\n\n## History\n\n[2 Commits](/facebookresearch/gismo/commits/main/)\n\n[](/facebookresearch/gismo/commits/main/)2 Commits\n\n## Folders and files\n\nName\n\nName\n\nLast commit message\n\nLast commit date\n\n[conf](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/conf \"conf\")\n\n[conf](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/conf \"conf\")\n\n[data/splits/recipe1m](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/data/splits/recipe1m \"This path skips through empty directories\")\n\n[data/splits/recipe1m](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/data/splits/recipe1m \"This path skips through empty directories\")\n\n[gismo](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/gismo \"gismo\")\n\n[gismo](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/gismo \"gismo\")\n\n[inv\\_cooking](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/inv_cooking \"inv_cooking\")\n\n[inv\\_cooking](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/inv_cooking \"inv_cooking\")\n\n[notebooks](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/notebooks \"notebooks\")\n\n[notebooks](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/notebooks \"notebooks\")\n\n[scripts](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/scripts \"scripts\")\n\n[scripts](/facebookresearch/gismo/tree/main/scripts \"scripts\")\n\n[.gitignore](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/.gitignore \".gitignore\")\n\n[.gitignore](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/.gitignore \".gitignore\")\n\n[CODE\\_OF\\_CONDUCT.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md \"CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\")\n\n[CODE\\_OF\\_CONDUCT.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md \"CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\")\n\n[CONTRIBUTING.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md \"CONTRIBUTING.md\")\n\n[CONTRIBUTING.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md \"CONTRIBUTING.md\")\n\n[LICENSE.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/LICENSE.md \"LICENSE.md\")\n\n[LICENSE.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/LICENSE.md \"LICENSE.md\")\n\n[Makefile](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/Makefile \"Makefile\")\n\n[Makefile](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/Makefile \"Makefile\")\n\n[README.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/README.md \"README.md\")\n\n[README.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/README.md \"README.md\")\n\n[environment\\_inv.yml](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/environment_inv.yml \"environment_inv.yml\")\n\n[environment\\_inv.yml](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/environment_inv.yml \"environment_inv.yml\")\n\n[eval.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/eval.py \"eval.py\")\n\n[eval.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/eval.py \"eval.py\")\n\n[preprocess.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/preprocess.py \"preprocess.py\")\n\n[preprocess.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/preprocess.py \"preprocess.py\")\n\n[requirements.txt](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/requirements.txt \"requirements.txt\")\n\n[requirements.txt](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/requirements.txt \"requirements.txt\")\n\n[requirements\\_dev.txt](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/requirements_dev.txt \"requirements_dev.txt\")\n\n[requirements\\_dev.txt](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/requirements_dev.txt \"requirements_dev.txt\")\n\n[setup.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/setup.py \"setup.py\")\n\n[setup.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/setup.py \"setup.py\")\n\n[train.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/train.py \"train.py\")\n\n[train.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/train.py \"train.py\")\n\n[visualize.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/visualize.py \"visualize.py\")\n\n[visualize.py](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/visualize.py \"visualize.py\")\n\nView all files\n\n## Repository files navigation\n\n-   [README](#)\n-   [Code of conduct](#)\n-   [Contributing](#)\n-   [License](#)\n-   [Security](#)\n\nMore items\n\n# InverseCooking 2.0: Graph-based Ingredient Substitution Module (GISMo)\n\n[](#inversecooking-20-graph-based-ingredient-substitution-module-gismo)\n\nCode to reproduce the experiments of [Learning to Substitute Ingredients in Recipes](https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.07960).\n\n  \n\n## Installation\n\n[](#installation)\n\nThis code uses Python 3.8.5 (Anaconda), PyTorch 1.7, Torchvision 0.8.1 and CUDA version 10.1.\n\nInstall PyTorch:\n\n```\nconda install -c pytorch pytorch=1.7.1 torchvision cudatoolkit=10.2\nconda install -c conda-forge -c fvcore -c iopath fvcore iopath\nconda install pytorch3d -c pytorch3d\n```\n\nInstall dependencies:\n\n```\npip install -r requirements.txt --upgrade\n```\n\nAdditional dependencies for developers (optional):\n\n```\npip install -r requirements_dev.txt --upgrade\npip install -e \".[dev]\"\n```\n\nSeting up NLTK punkt and Spacy (for pre-processing of datasets):\n\n```\npython -c \"import nltk; nltk.download('punkt')\"\npython3 -m spacy download en_core_web_lg\n```\n\nVerify that the install worked:\n\n```\npython -c \"import spacy; spacy.load('en_core_web_lg')\"\n```\n\n  \n\n## Datasets\n\n[](#datasets)\n\n#### Recipe1M\n\n[](#recipe1m)\n\nDownload [Recipe1M](http://im2recipe.csail.mit.edu/dataset/download) (registration required) and extract under `/path/to/recipe1m/`.\n\nThe contents of `/path/to/recipe1m/` should be the following:\n\n```\ndet_ingrs.json\nlayer1.json\nlayer2.json\nimages/\nimages/train\nimages/val\nimages/test\n```\n\nLink the dataset to your current folder (the other option is to modify \"path\" in the configuration of the dataset)\n\n```\nln -s /path/to/recipe1m/ data/recipe1m\n```\n\nPre-process the dataset with:\n\n```\npython preprocess.py dataset=recipe1m\n```\n\n  \n\n## Training ingredient substitution module\n\n[](#training-ingredient-substitution-module)\n\nPlease follow the instructions [here](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/gismo/README.md).\n\n## Training image-to-recipe\n\n[](#training-image-to-recipe)\n\n### Running experiments\n\n[](#running-experiments)\n\nTraining can be run as in the following example command:\n\n```\npython train.py task=im2recipe name=im2recipe\n```\n\nThis command will look for the definition of the experiment \"im2recipe\" in the configuration file \"conf/experiments/im2recipe.yaml\" and run this experiment.\n\nEvaluation can be run as in the following example command:\n\n```\npython eval.py task=im2recipe name=im2recipe\n```\n\n### Running on SLURM\n\n[](#running-on-slurm)\n\nRunning on SLURM requires only to add the SLURM configuration to the command line:\n\n```\npython train.py task=im2recipe name=im2recipe slurm=<SLURM_CONF>\n```\n\nExisting SLURM configurations can be found in the folder `conf/slurm/<SLURM_CONF>.yaml`. Feel free to add configurations for your specific cluster. You can find an example with `conf/slurm/devlab.yaml`.\n\n### Monitoring progress\n\n[](#monitoring-progress)\n\nCheck training progress with Tensorboard from the folder in which the checkpoint are saved:\n\n```\ntensorboard --logdir='.' --port=6006\n```\n\n  \n\n## Reproducing experiments\n\n[](#reproducing-experiments)\n\nTo train our best ViT-based model, and reproduce the numbers reported in the paper, follow the steps below.\n\n### Training\n\n[](#training)\n\nTrain the image-to-ingredient model:\n\n```\npython train.py task=im2ingr name=im2ingr_vit_16_ff_bce_cat_multi_level\n```\n\nOnce the job is finished, note the name of the folder in which it has been trained, for instance:\n\n```\nPATH_1=/path/to/im2ingr-im2ingr_vit_16_ff_bce_cat_multi_level\n```\n\nThen train the image-to-recipe model using the checkpoint of the image-to-ingredient model to initialize the image encoder:\n\n```\npython train.py task=im2recipe \\\n    name=im2recipe_vit16_multi_level \\\n    experiments.im2recipe.im2recipe_vit16_multi_level.pretrained_im2ingr.load_pretrained_from=<<PATH_1>>\n```\n\nOnce the job is finished, note the name of the folder in which it has been trained, for instance:\n\n```\nPATH_2=/path/to/im2recipe-im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_4\n```\n\n### Evaluation\n\n[](#evaluation)\n\nNow, we can evaluate the model, first on the recipe generation alone (using ground truth ingredients):\n\n```\npython eval.py task=im2recipe \\\n    dataset.eval_split=val_all \\\n    name=eval_im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_recipe_inference \\\n    eval_checkpoint_dir=<<PATH_2>>\n```\n\nThe the end-to-end pipeline from image to predicted ingredients and generated recipe:\n\n```\npython eval.py task=im2recipe \\\n    dataset.eval_split=val_all \\\n    name=eval_im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_full_inference \\\n    eval_checkpoint_dir=<<PATH_2>>\n```\n\nYou can also customize the evaluation to use a different evaluation split. To do so, change the flag `eval_split` in the command line to one of: `train`, `val` (subset of 5k samples from val\\_all), `val_all` or `test`.\n\n### Evaluation with GISMo\n\n[](#evaluation-with-gismo)\n\n[GISMo](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/gismo/README.md) model allows to provide substitution suggestion. For each of the validation inputs, this model will write potential substitutions. To evaluate the impact of substitutions generated by [GISMo](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/gismo/README.md) on the image-to-recipe pipeline, you can perform the following test.\n\nFirst, measure the perplexity of recipes with no substitutions (this command sub-select the samples of the validate set that do have substitutions):\n\n```\npython eval.py task=im2recipe \\\n    dataset.eval_split=val_all \\\n    name=eval_im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_recipe_inference \\\n    dataset.ablation.with_substitutions=True \\\n    eval_checkpoint_dir=<<PATH_2>>\n```\n\nThen, measure the perplexity of recipes with ground truth substitutions (on the same sub-set of the validation set):\n\n```\npython eval.py task=im2recipe \\\n    dataset.eval_split=val_all \\\n    name=eval_im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_recipe_inference \\\n    dataset.ablation.with_substitutions=True \\\n    eval_checkpoint_dir=<<PATH_2>> \\\n    experiments.im2recipe.eval_im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_recipe_inference.ingr_teachforce.test=use_substitutions\n```\n\nFinally, measure the perplexity of recipes with GISMO substitutions (on the same sub-set of the validation set):\n\n```\npython eval.py task=im2recipe \\\n    dataset.eval_split=val_all \\\n    name=eval_im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_recipe_inference \\\n    dataset.ablation.with_substitutions=True \\\n    eval_checkpoint_dir=<<PATH_2>> \\\n    experiments.im2recipe.eval_im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_recipe_inference.ingr_teachforce.test=use_substitutions \\\n    dataset.ablation.alternate_substitution_set=/path/to/gismo_output/val_output.pkl\n```\n\n  \n\n### Visualisation with GISMo\n\n[](#visualisation-with-gismo)\n\nThe following command line with run some basic visualisation and export the model to a format with which interactive interaction with GISMo will be possible:\n\n```\npython visualize.py task=im2recipe \\\n    dataset.ablation.with_substitutions=True \\\n    name=eval_im2recipe_vit16_multi_level_recipe_inference \\\n    eval_checkpoint_dir=<<PATH_2>>\n```\n\nAfter this command has completely, you should have a new `model_and_module.torch` file under the `PATH_2` folder.\n\nNow, run `jupyter lab` and go to `notebooks/InteractiveGismo.ipynb` and use this path to interact with GISMo!\n\n## Pre-trained models\n\n[](#pre-trained-models)\n\n-   Inverse Cooking: [model](https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/gismo/best.ckpt), [ingredients vocabulary](https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/gismo/final_recipe1m_vocab_ingrs.pkl), [recipes vocabulary](https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/gismo/final_recipe1m_vocab_toks.pkl), [titles vocabulary](https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/gismo/final_recipe1m_vocab_title.pkl)\n    \n-   GisMO: [model](https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/gismo/best_model.chkpnt)\n    \n\n## Contributing\n\n[](#contributing)\n\nSee [CONTRIBUTING.md](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n\n### Developer tools\n\n[](#developer-tools)\n\nThe following commands should be used prior to submitting a fix:\n\n-   `make format` to format all the files with and remove useless imports\n-   `make test` to ensure that all unit tests are green\n-   `make check` to run basic static checks on the codebase\n\n  \n\n## License\n\n[](#license)\n\nThe majority of ingredient-substitution is licensed under CC-BY-NC, see [LICENSE](/facebookresearch/gismo/blob/main/LICENSE.md) for details. However, portions of the project are available under separate license terms: dglteam, mltk, pytorch lightning, transformers, tokenizers, and timm are licensed under the Apache 2.0 license; hydra, inversecooking, tqdm, and spacy are licensed under the MIT License; pandas, scipy, and scikit-learn are licensed under the BSD 3-Clause New or Revised License.\n\n## About\n\ncompanion code for \"Learning to substitute Ingredients in Recipes\"\n\n### Resources\n\n[Readme](#readme-ov-file)\n\n[License](#License-1-ov-file)\n\n### Code of conduct\n\n[Code of conduct](/facebookresearch/gismo#coc-ov-file)\n\n### Contributing\n\n[Contributing](#contributing-ov-file)\n\n### Security policy\n\n[Security policy](#security-ov-file)\n\n[Activity](/facebookresearch/gismo/activity)\n\n[Custom properties](/facebookresearch/gismo/custom-properties)\n\n### Stars\n\n**27** stars\n\n### Watchers\n\n**2** watching\n\n### Forks\n\n[**5** forks](/facebookresearch/gismo/forks)\n\n[Report repository](/contact/report-content?content_url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Ffacebookresearch%2Fgismo&report=facebookresearch+%28user%29)\n\n## Releases\n\n## Packages\n\n## Contributors\n\n## Languages\n\n## Footer\n\n[](https://github.com)© 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n\n### Footer navigation\n\n-   [Terms](https://docs.github.com/site-policy/github-terms/github-terms-of-service)\n-   [Privacy](https:/