els like BERT and GPT can analyze large datasets to detect patterns in substitution, functional roles, and cultural associations that would be difficult to identify manually.\\nNLP-driven knowledge graphs have been applied to recipe recommendation and question-answering systems, especially when combined with structured resources such as nutrient or sensory databases [ 53 ]. The outputs of these models can also feed into predictive pipelines, adding contextual and cultural intelligence to formulation decisions.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/14/21/9675\",\n      \"title\": \"Incorporation of Chokeberry Pomace into Baked Products - MDPI\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Incorporation of Chokeberry Pomace into Baked Products - MDPI\\nThe sensory study showed that a substitution of 10% of typical flour resulted in products acceptable to potential consumers, but a higher\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://muckrack.com/luis-rita\",\n      \"title\": \"Luis Rita's Profile | The Startup, Nature, MDPI Journalist | Muck Rack\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2024-11-26\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Optimizing Ingredient Substitution Using Large Language Models to Enhance Phytochemical Content in Recipes\\nNov 26, 2024 | By Luis Rita , Luís Rita , Joshua Southern , Ivan Laponogov , Kyle Higgins | MDPI\\nAll articles published by MDPI are made immediately available worldwide under an open access license. No special permission is required to reuse all or part of the article published by MDPI, including figures and tables.\\n%0D%0A%0D%0A/link/eJgCDd/optimizing-ingredient-substitution-using-large-language-models-to-enhance-phytochemical-content-in-recipes&subject=Byline%20is%20for%20a%20different%20person%20with%20the%20same%20name%20as%20me)\\n* [Inaccurate duplicate grouping of articles.](mailto:hello@muckrack.com?body=Please remove my name from this article. %0D%0A%0D%0Ahttps://muc