    "content": "{\n  \"search_id\": \"search_2fa9e7bee9e26bf8ade0d55e81a04147\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://platform.tracxn.com/a/d/company/56cb0d95e4b036ef16088aab/hyperfood?utm_source=parallel&utm_medium=ai#a:about\",\n      \"title\": \"HYPERFOOD\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Name: HYPERFOOD | Website Url: http://hyperfood.co | Primary Sector: Food and Agriculture Tech | Primary Subsector: Food Tech | Stage: Unfunded | Founded Year: 2015 | Location Country: United Kingdom | Location State: England | Acquisitions As Acquirer Count: 0 | Other Taxonomy Tags: [\\\"Trending Themes in Food Tech\\\",\\\"Restaurant IT\\\",\\\"UK & Ireland Tech\\\",\\\"SaaS - UK & Ireland\\\",\\\"Restaurant SaaS\\\",\\\"Vertical SaaS\\\",\\\"Europe Tech\\\",\\\"Enterprise Tech - Europe\\\",\\\"Enterprise Tech - UK & Ireland\\\",\\\"Enterprise Applications\\\",\\\"SaaS\\\",\\\"SaaS - Europe\\\",\\\"Food and Agriculture SaaS\\\",\\\"Enterprise Software\\\",\\\"UK Tech\\\",\\\"SaaS -\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"http://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/899932/results\",\n      \"title\": \"Computational discovery and design of disease-beating nutrition | Hyperfoods | Project | Results | H2020 | CORDIS | European Commission\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2023-06-23\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Hyperfoods\\nGrant agreement ID: 899932\\nDOI Each project (from H2020 onwards) is attributed a Digital Object Identifier (DOI)\\n10.3030/899932\\nProject closed\\nEC signature date 30 March 2020\\nStart date 1 April 2020\\nEnd date 30 June 2022\\nFunded under\\n* EXCELLENT SCIENCE - European Research Council (ERC)\\nTotal cost The total amount of money invested in the project. The total cost includes EU contribution as well as other project costs not covered by EU funding. It is expressed in euros.\\nNo data\\nThe sum of the EU contributions of all participants in a project is equal to the grant amount.\\n€ 150 000,00\\nCoordinated by\\nIMPERIAL COLLEGE OF SCIENCE TECHNOLOGY AND MEDICINE United Kingdom\\nCORDIS provides links to public deliverables and publications of HORIZON projects.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/899932/reporting/it\",\n      \"title\": \"Computational discovery and design of disease-beating nutrition | H2020 | CORDIS | Commissione europea\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2020-04-03\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Informazioni relative al progetto\\nHyperfoods\\nID dell’accordo di sovvenzione: 899932\\nDOI Ad ogni progetto (da H2020 in poi) viene attribuito un Digital Object Identifier (DOI).\\n10.3030/899932\\nProgetto chiuso\\nData della firma CE 30 Marzo 2020\\nData di avvio 1 Aprile 2020\\nData di completamento 30 Giugno 2022\\nFinanziato da\\n* EXCELLENT SCIENCE - European Research Council (ERC)\\nCosto totale L’importo totale investito nel progetto. Il costo totale comprende il contributo dell’UE e altri costi del progetto non coperti dai finanziamenti dell’UE. È espresso in euro.\\nNessun dato\\nPeriodic Reporting for period 1 - Hyperfoods (Computational discovery and design of disease-beating nutrition)\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"http://www.cordis.europa.eu/search/it?q=%2Fproject%2Fkeywords%3D%22%20digital%20therapeutics%22\",\n      \"title\": \"Ricerca | CORDIS | Commissione europea\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Hyperfoods Computational discovery and design of disease-beating nutrition\\nID: 899932\\nDa: 1 Aprile 2020 al: 30 Giugno 2022\\nWith rapidly ageing populations, the world is experiencing an unsustainable healthcare and economic burden from chronic diseases such as cancer, cardiovascular, metabolic and neurodegenerative disorders. Diet and nutritional factors play an essential role in the prevention of...\\nCoordinato da: United Kingdom\\nProgramma: EXCELLENT SCIENCE - European Research Council (ERC)\\nUltimo aggiornamento: 23 Giugno 2023\\nAggiungi al mio fascicolo Progetto\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdpi.com/2304-8158/14/22/3919\",\n      \"title\": \"Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Ingredient Substitution in Food Systems: A Review and Conceptual Framework for Sensory, Functional, Nutritional, and Cultural Optimization\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2025-01-01\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"uptake is limited, with many studies still at proof-of-concept stages. Addressing these gaps is crucial for moving beyond theoretical architectures toward fully operational and scalable substitution systems.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7861309/\",\n      \"title\": \"\\n            Identifying Ingredient Substitutions Using a Knowledge Graph of Food - PMC\\n        \",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2025-01-21\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Improving ingredient substitution using formal concept analysis and adaptation of ingredient quantities with mixed linear optimization, Computer cooking contest workshop (Frankfurt, Germany: CEUR Workshop Proceedings; ). [ Google Scholar ]\\n12. Garg N., Sethupathy A., Tuwani R., Nk R., Dokania S., Iyer A. (2018).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/artificial-intelligence/articles/10.3389/frai.2020.621766/full\",\n      \"title\": \"Frontiers | Identifying Ingredient Substitutions Using a Knowledge Graph of Food\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2021-01-25\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Improving ingredient substitution using formal concept analysis and adaptation of ingredient quantities with mixed linear optimization, Computer cooking contest workshop. (Frankfurt, Germany: CEUR Workshop Proceedings).\\n* Google Scholar\\n* View reference in article\\n* 12\\nGarg N. Sethupathy A. Tuwani R. Nk R. Dokania S. Iyer A. (2018).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://mdpi-res.com/d_attachment/sensors/sensors-22-01095/article_deploy/sens